{
  "engine_notes": [
    "Offsets are calendar days from the trigger date (a written offer or an approved work-location change).",
    "Forward pass = earliest each step can happen. Backward pass = latest it can happen and still hit the required first office day.",
    "Slack is the difference. Negative slack anywhere means the runway is too short and something must give: the report date, a remote transition period, or the sequence itself.",
    "The terminal anchor is first_office_day. first_ca_paycheck floats after it and is informational.",
    "Durations are calendar days, deliberately not working days: movers, landlords and dogs do not observe business hours."
  ],
  "steps": [
